Prompts: Provisioning Trigger

Purpose:
  Define when and how automated provisioning is triggered
  after human approval of role assignments.

Triggers:
  SERVER_PROVISIONING:
    Condition: Backend role assigned AND scale > 1000 users
    Action: Provision cloud servers (AWS/GCP/Azure)
    Requires: Human approval
    Auto-select: Instance type based on scale

  DATABASE_PROVISIONING:
    Condition: Database role assigned
    Action: Provision database cluster
    Requires: Human approval
    Auto-select: DB type, size, replication

  CDN_PROVISIONING:
    Condition: Frontend role assigned AND global users
    Action: Provision CDN (CloudFront/Cloudflare)
    Requires: Human approval
    Auto-select: Regions based on user geography

  VIDEO_INFRASTRUCTURE:
    Condition: Video conferencing feature detected
    Action: Provision STUN/TURN servers
    Requires: Human approval
    Auto-select: Provider (Twilio/AWS/self-hosted)

  MONITORING:
    Condition: Production deployment
    Action: Provision monitoring (Prometheus/Grafana)
    Requires: Auto (no approval needed)
    Auto-select: Based on stack

Rules:
  [PT1] Provisioning MUST only trigger after human approval.
  [PT2] Provisioning MUST be logged in audit trail.
  [PT3] Provisioning MUST be reversible (terraform/destroy).
  [PT4] Cost estimates MUST be shown before provisioning.
  [PT5] Provisioning MUST follow security best practices.

State: +
